# The trial of pod-dns and pod-services in podnet, in one patch: pod-dns
# reads its default resolvers from pod-services, and both take the place of
# constants in the same files. src/resolve.rs stays as thin glue: podnet's
# settings of the resolver (the pins of --resolve and PODNET_RESOLVE, the
# DoH servers of pod-services with the JSON form, the family of the host
# first, the names last, A and AAAA both, NXDOMAIN asks the next operator,
# no cache, 5 s for each step, the roots of its context, its user agent);
# each dialer takes the resolver, whose DoH goes through the same proxy with
# no DoH for its own names. Each value of the relay, the edge, the quick
# tunnels, WARP, 1.1.1.1 and Pinggy is a read of pod-services. The record,
# the size of the files, the build, the bans and the sources of cargo-deny,
# clippy, the tests of the library, the integration tests that read DNS or
# a moved value, the fuzz targets with their lock, which follows the crates
# of the tree (at the tag, the consumer runs the same `cargo update -w` in
# fuzz/), rustfmt, each Rust toolchain of the workflows and build images
# against the rust-version of podcrates, and the binary for x86_64 musl,
# built with zig (a debug build: the release profile takes LTO), with
# podnet's static check of it.
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-size.py
cargo build -q
command -v cargo-deny > /dev/null || cargo install -q --locked cargo-deny
cargo deny --locked check bans sources
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podnet -p podnet-netns -- -D warnings
cargo test -q -p podnet --lib
cargo test -q -p podnet --test egress --test tls --test relay_reverse --test cli --test doctor --test api_surface --test connect --test docs --test update_umask
cargo update -q -w --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml
cargo check -q --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml --bins
cargo fmt --all --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
cargo zigbuild -q --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -p podnet --bin podnet
sh scripts/check-static.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podnet"
